@!internal

module nupp.runtime.provider.wasmstorage

--[[
State-local entry for `representation.cstorage` on linear memory.

The host must install `__nuppWasmHost` before this module is required. The module
passes that memory service to [](nupp.runtime.provider.wasmstoragefactory) once
and exports the resulting storage, integer, struct, and Wasm operations together.
A missing host fails module initialization.

The implementation reports `linear32`. Its allocations and pointers belong to
that host instance, and its integer operations must remain the same ones used by
[](nupp.runtime.int64). Worker lanes construct their own instance from their own
host; provider tables, closures, and memory handles are not transferred between
Lua states.
]]

local factory = require("nupp.runtime.provider.wasmstoragefactory")
local memory: any = assert(rawget(_G, "__nuppWasmHost"), "nupp: the Wasm memory host is not installed")
export = factory.new(memory)
